# 5. WAKE-WORD ACTIVATION — "HEY NOVA"

This is a major product feature.

Implement a browser-compatible wake-word system.

Activation phrase:

"Hey NOVA"

Alternative activation phrase:

"Hi NOVA"

Expected behavior:

- User enables wake-word activation.
- Browser requests microphone permission.
- The application starts a lightweight local wake-word detector.
- The detector continuously listens for the configured activation phrase.
- When the phrase is detected, NOVA activates.
- A visual animation confirms activation.
- The full voice assistant session starts.
- NOVA listens for the user's instruction.
- NOVA responds using natural speech.
- After completing the response, the application returns to the selected listening mode.

IMPORTANT TECHNICAL DESIGN:

Do not continuously send microphone audio to Gemini simply to detect the wake word.

Use a local wake-word detection engine wherever possible.

Investigate a suitable browser-compatible solution such as:
- A supported Porcupine Web SDK integration.
- Another compatible local wake-word engine.
- A lightweight local speech recognition alternative where supported.

Create an abstraction:

WakeWordManager

Responsibilities:
- Initialize detector.
- Load wake-word model.
- Manage microphone access.
- Detect activation.
- Stop detection.
- Handle microphone permissions.
- Handle unsupported browsers.
- Handle model-loading errors.
- Release audio resources.
- Provide activation callbacks.

Use a custom NOVA wake-word model only if the selected provider supports it and the required model is available.

Do not assume that browser speech recognition offers reliable always-on wake-word functionality.

Browser restrictions:

- Microphone access requires HTTPS or localhost.
- Microphone permission must be granted.
- Some browsers suspend audio processing when the page is backgrounded.
- Mobile operating systems may restrict continuous background microphone use.
- Browser tabs may be throttled.
- iOS may require a user gesture to start or resume audio.

Therefore:

Provide two modes.

MODE A — WAKE-WORD MODE

"Hey NOVA" activates the assistant when the browser and operating system permit background microphone processing.

MODE B — MANUAL MODE

The user presses the central microphone button to activate NOVA.

If wake-word functionality is unsupported or suspended, automatically provide a clear manual activation fallback.

Never claim that NOVA is listening in the background if the browser has suspended microphone processing.

Display a persistent but unobtrusive microphone status indicator.

Include a clear microphone disable button.

