# 17. LOCAL-FIRST MEMORY AND PRIVACY

This is a defining requirement of NOVA AI.

The default storage strategy must be local-first.

Use IndexedDB for:

- Conversation history.
- User preferences.
- Saved notes.
- Tasks.
- Local memory.
- Generated image metadata.
- Application settings.
- Workflow definitions.
- Local activity history.

Use Dexie.js if it simplifies IndexedDB management.

Do not require a cloud database for the core application.

The user should be able to use local memory without creating a cloud account, wherever the relevant application functionality permits.

## Local memory system

Create:

LocalMemoryManager

Responsibilities:

- Save user-approved memories.
- Retrieve relevant memories.
- Update memories.
- Delete memories.
- Search memory.
- Export memory.
- Import memory.
- Clear memory.

Memory categories:

- User preferences.
- Preferred language.
- Assistant settings.
- Frequently used websites.
- Project information.
- Business profile.
- Brand guidelines.
- Workflow preferences.
- Personal notes.

Do not automatically save sensitive information.

Ask for consent before storing long-term personal details.

## Privacy controls

Create a Privacy Center.

Include:

- Local memory status.
- Conversation history settings.
- Clear conversation history.
- Delete all local memory.
- Export data.
- Import backup.
- Disable persistent history.
- Disable wake-word detection.
- Stop microphone.
- Clear cached files.
- Cloud integration status.

Local storage is not equivalent to encrypted storage.

If sensitive local information is stored, offer optional client-side encryption using Web Crypto API.

Use a user-controlled passphrase or secure key-management design.

Do not store encryption keys in plain text beside encrypted data.

## Cloud usage

Cloud processing may be required for Gemini responses, search, image generation, email and external services.

Explain this clearly.

Before transmitting user files or private information to a provider, obtain permission where appropriate.

Do not claim that conversations are entirely private or offline when cloud AI services are being used.

Never send the entire local memory database to an AI provider.

Retrieve only relevant, user-authorized context for a particular request.

